We are given a set \( S \) of real numbers defined by the condition:
\[ x \in S \iff \lfloor x \rfloor \cdot (x - \lfloor x \rfloor) = a \cdot x^2 \]
where \( a \) is a rational number. We are also given that the sum of all elements in \( S \) is 420, and we need to prove that:
\[ \text{denominator of } a + \text{numerator of } a = 929 \]

